{
  "_about": "Hand-written map from words a reporter uses to what the code of a WordPress site can show for that feature (hooks, shortcodes, blocks, REST namespaces, AJAX actions, post types, script handles, well-known plugin slugs). Used to find WHICH components provide the feature. Every entry names the page it should be checked against. verified=false means the signals were written from the author's knowledge and have NOT been checked against that source; last_checked is null until someone does. A signal is a search term, not a proof. Hook signals must be specific to the feature: hooks nearly every plugin uses (init, wp_head, wp_footer, template_redirect, wp_enqueue_scripts, ...) are not signals, and a test enforces that.",
  "schema": 1,
